  "notes": "4-channel stereo headphone amplifier. Inputs A and B are balanced 6.35 mm TRS pairs; each headphone channel selects A or B. Each channel has a front and a rear 6.35 mm stereo headphone jack. LINK OUT A passes input A (without level/balance) to another AMP800. External 12 V DC supply (not listed). Controls from the Quick Start Guide: LEVEL, BALANCE, INPUT button (selects input channel A or B) and PHONES LEVEL per headphone channel, and the power button. LINK OUT A carries input A without any LEVEL or BALANCE setting. Not clear from the guide: whether the INPUT button also offers A+B (the A+B meter shows the combined level) - modelled as A or B. Assumption: PHONES LEVEL at 0 is silent.",
